From 19da6c36093331242c59da29faa94cf3fa63d1f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:22:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] unify: GT-BE98 and GT-BE19000 send plain Realtek switch
 command numbers

The 3006.102.10 source sends every /dev/rtkswitch command in an encoded
form that the rtl8372 driver of that drop decodes. GT-BE98 and GT-BE19000
are built here with the rtl8372 driver object of their own older GPL drop,
which takes the plain command number, as the 3006.102.8 line's source
passes it. With the encoded form no switch command got through on those two
models: the 2.5G WAN port's VLAN was not programmed, and port link, speed,
counters and the port address table read nothing.

shared.h: with RTCONFIG_REAPER_LEGACY_BLOBS (set for the four older-object
models only) RTKSWITCH_IOCTL(n) is the plain number, as the header already
has it for other models with an older driver. No other model is affected;
BQ16 and BQ16 Pro have no such switch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/shared/shared.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/shared/shared.h b/release/src/router/shared/shared.h
index c2e285a31f..1704f01c7a 100644
--- a/release/src/router/shared/shared.h
+++ b/release/src/router/shared/shared.h
@@ -3344,6 +3344,11 @@ extern int get_fa_dump(void);
 #include <sys/ioctl.h>
 #if defined(WIFI7_SDK_20241007) && (defined(RTBE58U_V2) || defined(TUFBE3600_V2) || defined(RTBE55))
 #define RTKSWITCH_IOCTL(n)	n
+#elif defined(RTCONFIG_REAPER_LEGACY_BLOBS)
+/* reaper 2026-11-15: a model built with the rtl8372 driver object of its older GPL drop (GT-BE98, GT-BE19000) -
+ * that driver takes the plain command number, as the 3006.102.8 source passes it (ioctl(fd, val, p)); the encoded
+ * form below is refused by it, so no switch command would get through (2.5G WAN VLAN, port status, counters). */
+#define RTKSWITCH_IOCTL(n)	n
 #else
 #define RTKSWITCH_IOC_MAGIC	'R'
 /* The NR field of _IO() is only 8 bits; n > 255 overflows into the TYPE field
-- 
